note right of Done
  What is already in the project:

  - Entity mappings exist for Store, User, Currency, Unit,
    Category, Product, Warehouse, WarehouseStock,
    Order, OrderEntry, Purchase and PurchaseEntry.
  - Admin CRUD exists for Store, Category, Product,
    Warehouse and WarehouseStock.
  - Fixtures exist for users, stores, currencies, units,
    category tree, product parameter names and many products.
  - Database migrations were rebuilt and schema validates.

  Important limitation:
  Some entities already have fields from Database.puml,
  but business workflows are not implemented yet.
  Example: Order has totals/currency/status fields,
  but no order CRUD and no stock posting logic.
end note

note right of Todo
  Recommended execution order:

  01_Core_Store_User_Reference_Data
  02_Catalog_Product_And_Pricing
  03_Parties_Customers_And_Suppliers
  04_Warehouse_Stock_Base
  05_Sales_Orders
  05.1_Order_Comments_And_History
  06_Purchases
  07_Payments
  08_Inventory_Documents_And_Movements
  09_Stock_Reservations
  10_Production
  11_Status_History_Audit_And_Deletions
  11.1_Universal_Status_Transition_Service

  The order matters because later modules depend on data
  and workflows from earlier modules.
end note

note bottom
  Implementation rules for all stages:

  1. Do not rename existing routes/selectors/form field names
     unless the task explicitly asks for it.
  2. Keep CRUD and business logic separate:
     controllers stay thin, managers/services perform posting,
     recalculation and workflow transitions.
  3. Add fixtures only for base dictionaries and repeatable test data.
  4. For stock and money flows, write tests before changing posting logic.
  5. After each stage run:
     - doctrine:schema:validate
     - lint:container
     - focused PHPUnit tests
     - fixtures load when fixtures changed
end note

@enduml
